[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Who's Who]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.27]Lesson 40 | 第40课
[00:01.99]Who's who | 谁是扮演者
[00:08.14]How did the policeman discover that the whole thing was a joke? | 警察是怎么发现整件事情是个玩笑的？
[00:14.21]It has never been explained why university students seem to enjoy practical jokes more than anyone else. | 为什么大学生似乎比任何人都更喜欢恶作剧，这一点从来没有人解释过。
[00:22.71]Students specialize in a particular type of practical joke: the hoax. | 大学生擅长一种特殊的恶作剧：戏弄人。
[00:28.79]Inviting the fire brigade to put out a nonexistent fire is a crude form of deception which no self-respecting student would ever indulde in. | 请消防队来扑灭一场不存在的火灾是一种拙劣的欺骗，有自尊心的大学生决不会参与。
[00:39.45]Students often create amusing situations which are funny to everyone except the victims. | 大学生们常常制造一些令除了受害者之外所有人都发笑的局面。
[00:46.93]When a student recently saw two workmen using a pneumatic drill outside his university, | 最近，一名大学生看见两名工人在他的大学门外使用风钻，
[00:54.24]he immediately telephoned the police and informed them that two students dressed up as workmen | 便立刻打电话给警察，说有两个装扮成工人的学生
[01:01.20]were tearing up the road with a pneumatic drill. | 正在用风钻破坏路面。
[01:04.69]As soon as he had hung up, he went over to the workmen and told them that if a policeman ordered them to go away, | 挂上电话后，他马上走到工人跟前，告诉他们如果有个警察来让他们离开，
[01:12.70]they were not to take him seriously. | 不要把他的话当真。
[01:15.42]He added that a student had dressed up as a policeman and was playing all sorts of silly jokes on people. | 他还补充说，有个学生经常装扮成警察，跟人们开各种愚蠢的玩笑。
[01:23.78]Both the police and the workmen were grateful to the student for this piece of advance information. | 警察和工人都感激这位学生事先通了消息。
[01:31.58]The student hid in an archway nearby where he could watch and hear everything that went on. | 这名大学生躲进了附近的一个拱门里，从那里可以看到并听到所发生的一切。
[01:38.73]Sure enough, a policeman arrived on the scene and politely asked the workmen to go away. | 果然，一名警察来到了现场，礼貌地请工人们离开。
[01:45.75]When he received a very rude reply from one of the workmen, he threatened to remove them by force. | 当其中一名工人出言粗鲁地回敬他时，他威胁说要用武力驱赶他们。
[01:53.54]The workmen told him to do as he pleased and the policeman telephoned for help. | 工人说悉听尊便，于是警察打电话请求支援。
[01:59.16]Shortly afterwards, 4 more policemen arrived and remonstrated with the workmen. | 不一会儿，又来了4名警察，跟工人们评理。
[02:05.79]As the men refused to stop working, the police attempted to seize the pneumatic drill. | 由于工人们拒绝停止干活，警察试图夺过风钻。
[02:12.84]The workmen struggled fiercely and one of them lost his temper. | 工人们激烈争夺，其中一人发了脾气。
[02:18.04]He threatened to call the police. | 他威胁说要叫警察。
[02:20.87]At this, the police pointed out ironically that this would hardly be necessary as the men were already under arrest. | 听到这话，警察讽刺地指出，这大可不必，因为他们已经被逮捕了。
[02:30.34]Pretending to speak seriously, one of the workmen asked if he might make a telephone call before being taken to the station. | 其中一名工人装出一本正经的样子，问在被带往警察局之前是否可以打一个电话。
[02:39.61]Permission was granted and a policeman accompanied him to a pay phone. | 获得了许可，一名警察陪他来到公用电话亭。
[02:45.09]Only when he saw that the man was actually telephoning the police did he realize that they had all been the victims of a hoax. | 直到看见那人真的在给警察打电话，他才明白他们全都上了一个恶作剧的当。
